          "why_needed": "An AI reading the code cold could think the NFKC/casefold steps are over-engineering and go back to the simpler lower(), which breaks fullwidth and ß matching. Or it could 'improve' matching by stripping accents, or by normalizing stored titles in place, which wrongly makes café match cafe or changes display data.",
