        "failure": null,
        "id": "D-FEAT-20261021-001-01",
        "body": "find_by_title in app/store.py matches by a comparison-only key from _title_key: unicodedata.normalize('NFKC', s).casefold() and then whitespace collapsed with ' '.join(s.split()). The first implementation used str.lower(). That fails for fullwidth text ('Ｆｏｏ' stays fullwidth under lower()) and for German sharp s ('Straße'.lower() never equals 'strasse'). Invariants: (1) normalize only the comparison keys and never write back to item['title'], because the test checks that items are deep-equal before and after; (2) return matches in input order; (3) do not strip accents: 'café' and 'cafe' must stay distinct, so NFKD plus combining-mark removal is wrong; (4) matching is exact on the key, not prefix or substring ('fo' matches nothing). Use `python3 -B` so no __pycache__ is written into the snapshotted tree. The check fails at 8b124f2 (lower()) and passes at 0ab39f5. That was worked out by reading the code; it was not run in this retrospective because Bash test execution was denied."
